"Find $t$, if $2{a}_{1}+t{a}_{2}=0$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$"] ["question-6154ace2-6af4-581c-9596-72c7ea4a622a" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $t$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+t{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 2[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ t[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\ t[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-16 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the first components, we get \n\n$$\n-4t=-16\\,⟹\\,t=4.\n$$\n\nBut then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-16 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]\\ne [\\begin{aligned}-16 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there is no $t$ such that \n $2{a}_{1}+t{a}_{2}=0.$"] ["question-6154ace2-6af4-581c-9596-72c7ea4a622a" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-a8913bcd-9ea3-5176-be5c-767230b5bdc3" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8913bcd-9ea3-5176-be5c-767230b5bdc3"] ["answer-e217e4b1-a0b0-5f52-9881-b8ba9a5204d2" :answer/id #uuid "e217e4b1-a0b0-5f52-9881-b8ba9a5204d2"] ["answer-e217e4b1-a0b0-5f52-9881-b8ba9a5204d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e217e4b1-a0b0-5f52-9881-b8ba9a5204d2" :answer/value "-2"] ["answer-c3245f41-6987-5e17-b6c5-0c173f25056e" :answer/id #uuid "c3245f41-6987-5e17-b6c5-0c173f25056e"] ["answer-c3245f41-6987-5e17-b6c5-0c173f25056e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c3245f41-6987-5e17-b6c5-0c173f25056e" :answer/value "-4"] ["answer-91df5346-a42d-5fd9-a5ba-0704fb0cc455" :answer/id #uuid "91df5346-a42